      "userJourney": "1. The Association anchors its trust registry on Verana's Verifiable Public Registry: two schemas, a digest-anchored governance framework, and its fee schedule (fees are example values).\n\n2. Members join through vetted, paid, renewable on-chain onboarding. Validated members receive their CEXA-VerifiedCounterparty credential. Members must already be Verifiable Services: the Association issues memberships, not identity.\n\n3. The customer's first exchange runs one full IDV check, seals the evidence bundle into their wallet, digest-bound, and issues CEXA-Kyc for free.\n\n4. On reuse, the wallet trust-resolves the requester and checks its VERIFIER accreditation before presenting. The verifier re-binds the person (passport NFC plus face match), receives the sealed evidence as its own CDD file, and pays the protocol-split fee: 0.90 to the original issuer, 0.10 to the Association. No phone home: the issuer never learns where the customer went\n\n5. Travel Rule desks read the counterparty credential from the member's DID, free\n\n6. Failures fail closed: a verifiable exchange outside the Association resolves TRUSTED and is still refused; a revoked credential dies at every member at the next check",
